nd sociability enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Empathy,_love,_and_sociability_enhancement"},{"name":"Feelings of interdependent opposites","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Feelings_of_interdependent_opposites"},{"name":"Feelings of predeterminism","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Feelings_of_predeterminism"},{"name":"Feelings of self-design","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Feelings_of_self-design"},{"name":"Geometry","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Geometry"},{"name":"Immersion enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Immersion_enhancement"},{"name":"Increased blood pressure","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Increased_blood_pressure"},{"name":"Increased heart rate","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Increased_heart_rate"},{"name":"Increased libido","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Increased_libido"},{"name":"Internal hallucinations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Internal_hallucinations"},{"name":"Memory suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Memory_suppression"},{"name":"Nausea","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Nausea"},{"name":"Novelty enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Novelty_enhancement"},{"name":"Pattern recognition enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pattern_recognition_enhancement"},{"name":"Personal bias suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Personal_bias_suppression"},{"name":"Perspective alterations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perspective_alterations"},{"name":"Physical euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Physical_euphoria"},{"name":"Pupil dilation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pupil_dilation"},{"name":"Rejuvenation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Rejuvenation"},{"name":"Scenarios and plots","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Scenarios_and_plots"},{"name":"Scenery slicing","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Scenery_slicing"},{"name":"Settings, sceneries, and landscapes","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Settings,_sceneries,_and_landscapes"},{"name":"Spontaneous tactile sensations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Spontaneous_tactile_sensations"},{"name":"Stimulation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Stimulation"},{"name":"Symmetrical texture repetition","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Symmetrical_texture_repetition"},{"name":"Synaesthesia","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Synaesthesia"},{"name":"Tactile enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tactile_enhancement"},{"name":"Teeth grinding","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Teeth_grinding"},{"name":"Thought acceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_acceleration"},{"name":"Thought connectivity","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_connectivity"},{"name":"Time distortion","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Time_distortion"},{"name":"Tracers","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tracers"},{"name":"Transformations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Transformations"},{"name":"Visual haze","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Visual_haze"},{"name":"Euphoria"},{"name":"Giggling"},{"name":"Empathy"},{"name":"Insight"},{"name":"Brightened color"},{"name":"Closed/open eye visuals"},{"name":"Enhanced tactile sensation"},{"name":"Mental/physical stimulation"},{"name":"Decreased appetite"},{"name":"Restlessness"},{"name":"Change in perception of time"},{"name":"Ego softening"},{"name":"Sweating/chills"},{"name":"Muscle tension"},{"name":"Confusion"},{"name":"Insomnia"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Lithium","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[{"title":"In vivo metabolism of 4-bromo-2,5-dimethoxyphenethylamine (2C-B) in the rat: identification of urinary metabolites","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11916016"}],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/2C-B"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/2c-b"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_2CB.shtml"},{"title":"PiHKAL Entry","description":"Alexander & Ann Shulgin phenethylamine monograph","url":"https://www.erowid.org/library/books_online/pihkal/pihkal020.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2C-B"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 2C-B","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q229942"},{"title":"維基百科","description":"zh:Encyclopedia article","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-tw/2C-B"}],"wikidata":"Q229942","formula":"C10H14BrNO2","molarMass":260.13,"pharmacology":{"text":"2C-B acts as a potent partial agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2 receptors, including of the serotonin 5-HT2A and 5-HT2C receptors and to a lesser extent of the serotonin 5-HT2B receptor. In one study, it had EC50 (Emax) values of 1.2 nM (101%) at the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor, 13 nM (97%) at the serotonin 5-HT2B receptor, and 0.63 nM (98%) at the serotonin 5-HT2C receptor.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"2C-B","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2C-B#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Serotonin receptor modulator; Serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen; stimulant; Entactogen","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"1.2–2.5 hours"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Liver (MAO and CYP450)"},{"what":"turnsInto","says":"BDMPE, BDMPAA, BDMBA, and others"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Urine"}],"figures":"2C-B"},"uses":{"text":"The drug is used as a recreational drug and is usually taken orally. 2C-B was developed by Alexander Shulgin in 1974 and was described by him in the scientific literature in 1975. The drug emerged as a novel recreational designer drug and MDMA (ecstasy) substitute in the mid-1980s.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"2C-B","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2C-B","brands":"Erox; Nexus; Perfomax","routes":"Oral, insufflation","figures":"2C-B"},"sideEffects":{"text":"The adverse effects of 2C-B have been studied. They have been reported to include difficulty focusing gaze, trembling, sweating, nausea, abdominal pain, tachycardia, jaw clenching, difficulty breathing, coughing, diarrhea, dizziness, muscle or joint pain, tenseness, confusion, psychomotor slowing, and spatial memory impairment, among others. 2C-B produces much lower rates of fear and anxiety than other serotonergic psychedelics like psilocybin and LSD.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"2C-B","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2C-B#Side_effects"},"summaryZh":"2,5-二甲氧基-4-溴苯乙胺，俗稱六角，是一種2C系列的致幻劑，由亞歷山大·舒爾金於1974年合成，其製備與應用劑量在PiHKAL一書中均有闡明。可經口服或吸入途徑給藥。"}